,"content":"We have a &quot;starter&quot; session of gameplay that will flesh out the individuals who will be filling the pages with comments. Fat Daddy, my co author, is an amazing writer. We both lean towards what some would consider shock horror. Rob Zombie would probably give two thumbs up to most of our scribblings. We understand that most of the context will need to be edited for a more mainstream audience. Unless we find another platform. We have been kicking around the idea of seeing if the owners would consider publishing our work as canon.<br /> <br /> Any advice on where to start such an ambitious undertaking would be greatly appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27330-valairius","name":"Valairius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-13T18:33:12-07:00","id":1476352,"title":"","content":"The Demon Seed Collection, DtD, is supposed to have something dealing with Baltimore. Gonna do some Reading tonight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27330-valairius","name":"Valairius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T10:28:12-07:00","id":1482168,"title":"","content":"David Simon's Homicide: A Year on the Killing Streets is listed as inspirational material for Werewolf: The Forsaken.<br /> <br /> I could see a The Wire type narrative where you play out different stories and game lines dealing with a similar situation and setting. Such as Season 1: Demon; Season 2: Mage; Season 3: Werewolf. Or if you wante